"plookup: A simplified polynomial protocol for lookup tables (https://eprint.iacr.org/2020/315)\nciteturn6view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2020/315\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 70\nL0: # What a lovely hat\nL1: #### Is it made out of 【0†tin foil†iacr.org】?\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Cryptology ePrint Archive】\nL4: \nL5:   * 【2†Papers】 Updates from the last:\nL6:     * 【3†7 days】\nL7:     * 【4†31 days】\nL8:     * 【5†6 months】\nL9:     * 【6†365 days】\nL10:     * * * *\nL11: \nL12:     * 【7†Listing by year】\nL13:     * 【8†All papers】\nL14:     * 【9†Compact view】\nL15:     * 【10†Subscribe†www.iacr.org】\nL16:     * * * *\nL17: \nL18:     * 【11†How to cite】\nL19:     * * * *\nL20:     * 【12†Harvesting metadata】\nL21:   * 【2†Submissions】\nL22:     * 【13†Submit a paper】\nL23:     * 【14†Revise or withdraw a paper】\nL24:     * 【15†Acceptance and publishing conditions】\nL25: \nL26: 【16†Image: Search Button】\nL27: \nL28: [Input] [Button: Search ]\nL29: #### Paper 2020/315\nL30: \nL31: ### 【17†plookup: A simplified polynomial protocol for lookup tables】\nL32: \nL33: Ariel Gabizon and Zachary J. Williamson\nL34: ##### Abstract\nL35: We present a protocol for checking the values of a committed polynomial $f\\in \\mathbb{F}_{<n}[X]$ over a multiplicative subgroup $H\\subset \\mathbb{F}$ of size $n$, are contained in the values of a table $t\\in \\mathbb{F}^d$. Our protocol can be viewed as a simplification of one from Bootle et. al [BCGJM, ASIACRYPT 2018] for a similar problem, with potential efficiency improvements when $d\\leq n$.\nL36: In particular, [BCGJM]'s protocol requires comitting to several auxiliary polynomials of degree $d\\cdot \\log n$, whereas ours requires three commitments to auxiliary polynomials of degree $n$, which can be much smaller in the case $d\\sim n$. One common use case of this primitive in the zk-SNARK setting is a ``batched range proof'', where one wishes to check all of $f$'s values on $H$ are in a range $[0,\\ldots,M]$.\nL37: We present a slightly optimized protocol for this special case, and pose improving it as an open problem.\nL38: Note: typo, ack: Luke Pearson\nL39: ##### Metadata\nL40: \nL41: Available format(s)\nL42:     【17†PDF】\nL43: Publication info\nL44:     Preprint. MINOR revision.\nL45: Keywords\nL46:     【18†zk-SNARKs】【19†Polynomial Commitment Schemes】\nL47: Contact author(s)\nL48:     ariel @ aztecprotocol com\nL49: History\nL50:     2020-11-20: last of 4 revisions\nL51:     2020-03-15: received\nL52:     【20†See all versions】\nL53: Short URL\nL54:     【21†https://ia.cr/2020/315†ia.cr】\nL55: License\nL56: \nL57: 【22†CC BY†creativecommons.org】\nL58: BibTeX 【23†Image】Copy to clipboard\nL59: \nL60:     @misc{cryptoeprint:2020/315,\nL61:           author = {Ariel Gabizon and Zachary J.  Williamson},\nL62:           title = {plookup: A simplified polynomial protocol for lookup tables},\nL63:           howpublished = {Cryptology {ePrint} Archive, Paper 2020/315},\nL64:           year = {2020},\nL65:           url = {https://eprint.iacr.org/2020/315}\nL66:     }\nL67: \nL68: \nL69: Note: In order to protect the privacy of readers, eprint.iacr.org does not use cookies or embedded third party content.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nzkllm-ccs2024/LICENSE at main · jvhs0706/zkllm-ccs2024 · GitHub (https://github.com/jvhs0706/zkllm-ccs2024/blob/main/LICENSE)\nciteturn6view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/jvhs0706/zkllm-ccs2024/blob/main/LICENSE\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 264\nL0: 【0†Skip to content】\nL1: ## Navigation Menu\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Sign in】\nL4: \nL5: Appearance settings\nL6: \nL7:   * Platform\nL8: \nL9:     * AI CODE CREATION\nL10:       * 【2†GitHub CopilotWrite better code with AI】\nL11:       * 【3†GitHub Copilot appDirect agents from issue to merge】\nL12:       * 【4†MCP RegistryIntegrate 